{
  "memo": {
    "recommendation": "Prioritize usability next quarter, led by the ad load complaints (usability.ads), with the premium paywall as a close companion issue and playback crashes as the leading second option.",
    "memo_markdown": "## Recommendation\n\nFocus next quarter on usability, specifically the ad load issue: \"Too many ads interrupt listening experience\" has 2,842 complaints [C005] and a priority score of 5,892 [C008]. It is the largest classified, specific issue. The premium paywall (billing) should be scoped alongside it, since both concern the free-tier experience.\n\nThe generic \"General dissatisfaction\" bucket ranks first at 48,110 [C004], but it is non-specific venting (for example, review 1a43d900-7a6f-4952-b338-b1c7fb58e312) and cannot be acted on, so I exclude it.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Ads: 2,842 complaints [C005], mean severity 2.073188 [C007]. Users describe ads after each song (review cf7cb282-1a38-4a5f-a733-c41bf2926117) and frequent interruptions (review fa5eba46-75b8-4aba-8efd-a0e47c186906).\n- Usability roll-up figures: 3,467 complaints, severity sum 7,546, across 6 issues.\n- Secondary usability items: shuffle controls at 231 complaints [C021] and priority 634 [C024]; this is a smaller, discrete fix (review c747a3ba-29ec-4188-b5c3-38d662a84ae6).\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **Billing/support:** the premium paywall has 854 complaints [C009] and priority 2,515 [C012], with higher mean severity 2.944965 [C011]. It is a strong second and is linked to ads strategically (review 88cc8f74-0622-4064-b652-894fe63e1fd6). Roll-up: billing 1,094 complaints, severity sum 3,120. Support alone has only 9 complaints (roll-up).\n- **Playback:** crashes have 216 complaints [C013], priority 786 [C016] and high mean severity 3.638889 [C015] (review 647975bc-5143-4c8f-a38e-48b4acfe2916). Roll-up: 890 complaints, severity sum 2,807. It ranks lower on volume but is the best candidate if reliability is the goal.\n- **Access:** login failure has 152 complaints [C029] with the highest severity, 3.907895 [C031], and priority 594 [C032] (review 9d0cf6e4-f98d-46e7-a606-efeb713dbd47). Roll-up: access 183 complaints. Low volume, but a cheap, severe fix.\n\n## Risks and limitations\n\nCoverage: only about 19.98% of source rows (131,976 of 660,622) were classified; 528,646 were quarantined and unclassified rows are excluded from all counts. Reviews are self-selected public app-store text from May 2022 to Nov 2023, so counts are not prevalence. Severity is a model-assigned score. Ads and paywall are likely business-model tradeoffs, not just defects, and quotes with uninstall language show stated intent, not observed churn. No revenue impact is measured.\n\n## Next steps\n\n1. Have product and monetization review whether ad frequency or placement can change without hurting revenue.\n2. Scope the paywall messaging and gating of basic features jointly.\n3. Run a small parallel fix for login failures and crashes given their severity.\n4. Validate the classification on a sample of the unclassified rows to check for bias.",
